<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first</p>
<p>division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>15 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta)</p>
<p>14 - Abel Balbo (Roma), Vincenzo Montella (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>13 - Roberto Mancini (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>12 - Marcelo Otero (Vicenza)</p>
<p>11 - Youri Djorkaeff (Inter)</p>
<p>10 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p>9 - Enrico Chiesa (Parma), Sandro Tovalieri (Cagliari), George</p>
<p>Weah (Milan), Paolo Poggi (Udinese)</p>
<p>8 - Alessandro Del Piero and Michele Padovano (both Juventus),</p>
<p>Igor Kolyvanov (Bologna), Pasquale Luiso (Piacenza)</p>
<p>7 - Oliver Bierhoff (Udinese), Filippo Maniero (Verona), Marco</p>
<p>Negri (Perugia)</p>
<p>6 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Marco Amoroso (Udinese),  Luis</p>
<p>Oliveira and Anselmo Robbiati (both Fiorentina)</p>
<p>5 - Demetrio Albertini (Milan), Nicola Caccia, Andre Cruz and</p>
<p>Fabio Pecchia (all Napoli), Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria),</p>
<p>Roberto Murgita (Vicenza), Roberto Muzzi (Cagliari), Igor</p>
<p>Simutenkov (Reggiana)</p>
</text>
